  1369	Phase 2 unwinding
  1370	-----------------
  1371	
  1372	In phase 2, the stack is really unwound and cleanups are run.
  1373	
  1374	The VRS content at the start of phase 2 is that which existed at the
  1375	start of the call to \_Unwind\_RaiseException. Unwinding will proceed
  1376	frame by frame until a personality routine indicates it should stop, or
  1377	an uncontinuable error is encountered.
  1378	
  1379	.. note::
  1380	
  1381	   Statically detectable errors should be found during phase 1, allowing
  1382	   the throwing language to make a language-dependent response.
  1383	
  1384	The details are as follows:
  1385	
  1386	1. At the start of each new frame, \_Unwind\_Next\_Frame is entered with
  1387	   a pointer to the UCB. It searches the index table for the entry E
  1388	   that matches the return address (in VRS[r15]). If no matching entry
  1389	   is found, or if the entry contains the special bitpattern
  1390	   EXIDX\_CANTUNWIND (see `Index table entries`_), the unwinder will call abort(). Otherwise
  1391	   the personality routine (PR) for the frame is obtained via E, and the
  1392	   unwinder initializes the UCB pr\_cache substructure. The unwinder
  1393	   must then preserve VRS[r15] by some means, as the value may be needed
  1394	   again after performing any cleanup initiated by the PR. Finally it
  1395	   calls the PR, passing state \_US\_UNWIND\_FRAME\_STARTING, the UCB
  1396	   pointer, and an \_Unwind\_Context pointer for VRS access.
  1397	
  1398	   At this point:
  1399	
  1400	   - The PR has just been entered for the first time for this frame.
  1401	
  1402	   - The UCB pr\_cache and barrier\_cache substructures are valid.
